  "live_records": {
    "q-331950": {
      "dom_id": "step-q331950",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)=2 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]-3{X}_{2}(s) & =2 \\\\ 4(s-1)-(s-1)^{2}{X}_{2}(s)-6{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-[(s-1)^{2}+6]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 4(s-1)-({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =4-4(s-1) \\\\ -({s}^{2}-2s+7){X}_{2}(s) & =-4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-(s-1)\\cdot \\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}-2s+7)-(s-1)\\cdot 4(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-8s+28-4(s-1)(s-2)}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s+20}{2({s}^{2}-2s+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(s+5)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4(s-2)}{{s}^{2}-2s+7}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
