    "q-332026": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332026",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]+3{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ (s-2)[-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+6{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -2(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-6]{X}_{2}(s) & =8 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s){X}_{2}(s) & =8+2(s-2) \\\\ -s(s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2s+4 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2s(s+5)+2(s-3)(s+2)}{2s(s-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-2(s+2)}{s(s-5)}.\n$$",
