    "q-332388": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332388",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,{e}^{5t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{5\\cdot t} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{2t}+{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
